If you had burned Elbereth with the wand, it would not erode due to
fighting (or anything else). If you are sure you did not move off the
square, or disrupt the message by teleporting it, polymorphing it, or
overwriting it, then I suspect that your wand of fire was out of
charges when you tried to engrave with it, and you merely wrote in the
dust instead. Dust-writing will erode over time, even if you stay
perfectly still; thus the recommendation to levitate over it. Other
things that can cause Elbereth to fail are monsters which have been
blinded, and, IIRC, certain odd cases involving displacement, but
neither would be likely to affect all the adjacent monsters at once.

I have no experience with Slash'Em, but it sounds like your situation
could have been helped materially by a scroll of earth (boulder fort)
and/or a wand of teleport. A look at the Wiki suggests that in
Slash'Em you can use lightsabers to burn permanent Elbereth, which
might have been helpful too.


